    "system": "You read one page of a vendor document for pharmaceutical equipment: a FAT or SAT protocol and report, a datasheet or a certificate. Report only what the page prints.\nsite_approved_on: the date the customer site approved the protocol before execution, when the page prints that approval with a date; null otherwise (also when the site's approval is blank or only the vendor signed).\nexecuted_on: the date the tests were executed, when the page prints it; else null.\nFor both: date exactly as printed, and a quote that holds it.\nsteps: every test step on the page. step: its number exactly as printed; test: what it tests; acceptance: the acceptance criterion as printed; observed: the recorded result as printed (the measured value, not the pass/fail mark); result: pass, fail or none as recorded.\nrows: every design or certified value on a datasheet or certificate. name: the row label as printed; printed: the value as printed.\nvalue: the value as normalised data.\n- range: a sweep or interval (min and/or max); number: one reading; text: a material, type or other text, exactly as printed; present: a feature, function or document, with present true when it is there and works, false when it is absent or fails; none: no value you can read with certainty.\n- unit: a short English unit symbol such as mm, kN, rpm, min, bar or °C, as for the URS; null when there is none.\nquote: a verbatim excerpt of the page, at most 200 characters, holding the step number and its observed result, or the row label and its value. Copy characters exactly; never paraphrase or translate. If the page has none, return empty lists.",
    "user": "Document FAT-TP201-M, revision 0, page 2.\n\n<page>\nStep Test Acceptance criterion Result Pass/ Fail\nFAT-M-14 Check the spare parts list and as-built drawings. Present and functional Present and functional Pass\n4. Deviations\nNone recorded.\n5. Execution\nRole Name Company Signature Date\nExecuted by Markus Brandt Pressora Maschinenbau GmbH Signed electronically 01-Feb-2026\nWitnessed by Agus Setiawan Customer (site) Signed electronically 01-Feb-2026\n</page>"
